  "findings": [
    "In tested native backends, ten wakes from one update or ten separate systems produce one follow-up update, not ten recursive updates.",
    "PR23957 removes the no-redraw service stall in this controlled setup.",
    "Continuous self-waking sustains rapid updates, while independent event-loop markers and Last schedules still progress.",
    "App-side 16 ms service pacing reduces sustained feedback to 33 updates in each measured run; no trailing delivery loss or idle updates observed."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Windows results pending; browser/WASM not tested.",
    "No physical window minimization, occlusion, focus, resizing or input qualification.",
    "Not a full application CPU or GPU benchmark.",
    "No conclusion about prior revisions of PR23957 or all event-loop orderings.",
    "16 ms is a Limo application policy, not a proposed Bevy default."
  ],
  "possible_upstream_design": "Consider opt-in minimum explicit-wake spacing in reactive mode, disabled by default, with first idle wake prompt, one retained trailing wake, independent timer delivery without redraw, respect for react_to_user_events, no throttle of OS input/redraw, and explicit shutdown/lifecycle semantics. Keep design discussion separate from the wake correctness fix.",
  "upstream_posting": "No upstream comment posted; user will write it later under Bevy contribution policy."
